From 36ed799093edb506f32b5889b9404b9b21706a31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 22:29:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(terminal): canonicalize secure environment identity

Route terminal, file, search, patch, execute-code, process, environment lookup,
and cleanup through one opaque environment key. The previous task-only and
session-aware mappings could create state under one key and query or tear it
down under another, causing cross-conversation aliasing, empty process lists,
and leaked environments.

Resolve CWD and process ownership from the trusted raw gateway session key
rather than the durable transcript identifier. Capture the canonical key and
raw owner at turn start so transcript rotation cannot retarget cleanup, and
retain shared environments until their final raw owner leaves.

Keep writes beneath the immutable trusted workspace root, including canonical
Darwin temporary workspaces, without allowing a mutable CWD to bypass sensitive
system-path denial. Broker authority binding remains in the following patch so
this cross-surface identity and ownership contract stays backend-independent.
